# L0 / B011 — instruction-structure checker, .editorconfig, .gitignore.

C X26 EX - | MUST (checker-enforced) | Instruction inventory and model integrity: the required workflow skills (project-structure, verify, code-review, build-fix, custom-settings, git-workflow, security-scan, add-dependency, architecture-decision, template-maintenance) and knowledge skills (ef-core, http-api, aspnet-error-handling, dotnet-testing, logging, httpclient-factory, configuration, dependency-injection, caching, swagger, api-versioning, health-check, docker, ci-cd, angular, modern-csharp, authentication) exist with frontmatter name equal to the directory and a description; no standalone serilog or resilience skill; agents declare name and description; CLAUDE.md is Level 0 and imports the two stratified decision summaries (1-architecture/overview.md, 3-project/decisions.md) with resolving imports; no 'Kind:' classification and no manifests, capability contracts or slots under .claude; file, skill, agent and routed-workflow references resolve; skill-private references are used only by their owning skill. | template maintenance | The instruction map may list private references. | Inventory and model invariants of the L0 template; no oracle policy requires particular instruction artifacts, imports or forbids other instruction models' constructs. | Adding a capabilities/ directory, a standalone resilience skill or a Kind: header fails the checker.

